{#
  Ask bar for a static content page — the conversation footer's twin.

  Reuses .c-jonson__footer's classes so the layout, input and submit come for free;
  --light recolours it for the cream slab (see _jonson.scss).

  The back arrow carries data-wipe-thread, exactly as the conversation footer's does.
  It has to: without it the arrow navigates to `/`, thread-memory finds the snapshot
  and redraws the old conversation, so the same icon in the same corner went home from
  one page and back into the chat from another. It was the front door on the green
  pages and a back button on the cream ones, with nothing to tell them apart.

  The cost is a real one — leaving a case study this way ends the conversation rather
  than parking it. That's the trade for the arrow meaning one thing. Browser-back still
  returns to the thread intact, because a wipe only happens on a deliberate click.

  The form doesn't post — ask-handoff.js intercepts it, stashes the question and sends
  the visitor to the homepage, which asks it on arrival. Jonson only exists there, so
  a form posting from here would have nowhere to render.

  Optional: placeholder — defaults to the conversation's own wording.
            up          — a URL: adds a back button after the home one that goes up a
                          level (a note → the notes index). Plain navigation, no wipe:
                          going up a level isn't leaving the site's conversation.
            upLabel     — its accessible name; defaults to "Back".
#}
{# The "lost for words?" nudge tucked under the input — the front door's, reused,
   band and all: it slides out from behind the field on hover or focus, the
   homepage single's `prompts` land in the input, its `suggestions` reword the
   button. Rendered hidden; lost-for-words.js reveals it. data-prompt-scope is
   how the script finds this bar's input. #}
{# On a note or case study the drawer holds the page's own questions (its
   `prompts` rows, written on publish by the jonson module — see
   services\NoteMemory) and nothing else: the homepage's default set is the
   fallback for a page that has none (too thin to have been given any). #}
{% set home = craft.entries().section('homepage').status('live').one() %}
{% set own = (entry ?? null) and (entry.prompts ?? null) ? entry.prompts|map(row => row.prompt|trim)|filter(p => p) : [] %}
{% set defaults = home ? (home.prompts ?? [])|map(row => row.prompt|trim)|filter(p => p) : [] %}
{% set prompts = own|length ? own : defaults %}
{% set nudges = home ? (home.suggestions ?? [])|map(row => row.suggestions|trim)|filter(n => n) : [] %}
<footer class="c-jonson__footer c-jonson__footer--light" data-prompt-scope>
    {# The buttons share one grid cell (the left gutter, from md) as a row. #}
    <div class="c-jonson__nav">
    <a class="c-jonson__home" href="{{ siteUrl('') }}" aria-label="{{ siteName }}: Home" data-wipe-thread>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M11.47 3.841a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06 0l8.69 8.69a.75.75 0 1 0 1.06-1.061l-8.689-8.69a2.25 2.25 0 0 0-3.182 0l-8.69 8.69a.75.75 0 1 0 1.061 1.06l8.69-8.689Z"/>
            <path d="m12 5.432 8.159 8.159c.03.03.06.058.091.086v6.198c0 1.035-.84 1.875-1.875 1.875H15a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75v-4.5a.75.75 0 0 0-.75-.75h-3a.75.75 0 0 0-.75.75V21a.75.75 0 0 1-.75.75H5.625a1.875 1.875 0 0 1-1.875-1.875v-6.198a2.29 2.29 0 0 0 .091-.086L12 5.432Z"/>
        </svg>
    </a>
    {% if up is defined and up %}
        <a class="c-jonson__home c-jonson__home--up" href="{{ up }}" aria-label="{{ upLabel ?? 'Back' }}">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <path d="M19 12H5M11 6l-6 6 6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
        </a>
    {% endif %}
    </div>
    {# The field wrapper: holds the form and, tucked behind it, the band with the
       nudge — see .c-jonson__field. #}
    <div class="c-jonson__field" data-lost-for-words-field>
    <form class="c-jonson__form" method="get" action="{{ siteUrl('') }}" data-jonson-handoff>
        {# Which page the question was asked from. The handoff carries it to the
           Jonson page and on to the ask endpoint, which puts the page's text in
           front of the model — "why did you make the plugin bring its own HTML?"
           means nothing without the note it was asked under. #}
        {% if (entry ?? null) and entry.id %}
            <input type="hidden" name="from" value="{{ entry.id }}">
        {% endif %}
        <input
            class="c-jonson__input"
            type="text"
            name="question"
            placeholder="{{ placeholder ?? 'Ask me any question...' }}"
            {# No ellipsis on the label — it's read aloud, where trailing dots are
               noise rather than an invitation. #}
            aria-label="{{ placeholder ?? 'Ask me any question' }}"
            {# Matches AskController::MAX_QUESTION_CHARS. A courtesy, not a control —
               the server truncates regardless, since anything can post to the endpoint.
               This just stops an honest paste from being silently cut later. #}
            maxlength="1000"
            autocomplete="off"
            required
            data-jonson-input
        >
        <button class="c-jonson__submit" type="submit" aria-label="Submit">
            {# Sparkles, not an arrow: this submits a question to Jonson, not a form. Filled
               with currentColor, which the submit's own rule sets white on the red. #}
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M9 4.5a.75.75 0 0 1 .721.544l.813 2.846a3.75 3.75 0 0 0 2.576 2.576l2.846.813a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.442l-2.846.813a3.75 3.75 0 0 0-2.576 2.576l-.813 2.846a.75.75 0 0 1-1.442 0l-.813-2.846a3.75 3.75 0 0 0-2.576-2.576l-2.846-.813a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.442l2.846-.813A3.75 3.75 0 0 0 7.466 7.89l.813-2.846A.75.75 0 0 1 9 4.5ZM18 1.5a.75.75 0 0 1 .728.568l.258 1.036c.236.94.97 1.674 1.91 1.91l1.036.258a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.456l-1.036.258c-.94.236-1.674.97-1.91 1.91l-.258 1.036a.75.75 0 0 1-1.456 0l-.258-1.036a2.625 2.625 0 0 0-1.91-1.91l-1.036-.258a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.456l1.036-.258a2.625 2.625 0 0 0 1.91-1.91l.258-1.036A.75.75 0 0 1 18 1.5ZM16.5 15a.75.75 0 0 1 .712.513l.394 1.183c.15.447.5.799.948.948l1.183.395a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.422l-1.183.395c-.447.15-.799.5-.948.948l-.395 1.183a.75.75 0 0 1-1.422 0l-.395-1.183a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-.948-.948l-1.183-.395a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.422l1.183-.395c.447-.15.799-.5.948-.948l.395-1.183A.75.75 0 0 1 16.5 15Z"/>
            </svg>
        </button>
    </form>
    {% if prompts|length %}
        {# The band behind the field: one box that holds two panels — the nudge's
           label, and every prompt as a chip. Clicking the nudge slides the label
           out to the left and the chips in from the right while the band grows to
           fit them (see .c-jonson__band and lost-for-words.js). Picking a chip
           types it into the field. The button ships hidden; the script reveals it. #}
        <div class="c-jonson__band" data-lost-for-words-band>
            <div class="c-jonson__band-label">
                <button
                    class="c-jonson__prompt"
                    type="button"
                    hidden
                    data-lost-for-words='{{ prompts|values|json_encode|raw }}'
                    data-lost-for-words-own="{{ own|length }}"
                    data-lost-for-words-labels='{{ nudges|values|json_encode|raw }}'
                    aria-expanded="false"
                    aria-controls="lfw-{{ (entry ?? null) ? entry.id : 'page' }}"
                >{{ nudges|first|default('Stuck for something to ask?') }}</button>
            </div>
            <div class="c-jonson__band-chips" id="lfw-{{ (entry ?? null) ? entry.id : 'page' }}" hidden data-lost-for-words-drawer>
            <ul class="c-jonson__drawer-items">
                {% for p in prompts %}
                    <li class="c-jonson__drawer-item"><button type="button" class="c-jonson__suggestion c-jonson__drawer-chip" data-prompt="{{ p }}">{{ p }}</button></li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
    </div>
</footer>
